WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.752 --> 00:00:02.900
- Thanks to Indochino for
keeping LegalEagle in the air

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.990
and helping me look fly.

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:07.240
If you were taking bets on
what President Trump would do

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.440
after being acquitted of
impeachment in the Senate,

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.250
and you said meddle in the affairs

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.380
of the Department of Justice

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:15.100
in a way that would make
Richard Nixon blush,

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:18.430
well, you win, yay!

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:20.720
As you probably know,
Attorney General Barr

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.480
has begun overtly inserting
himself into the DOJ cases

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.610
that directly affect the president.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.550
That interference caused four prosecutors

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.320
at the DOJ to withdraw from
the case of Roger Stone,

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.860
and one resigned from the DOJ entirely.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:35.330
This is not normal.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:38.630
It's Nixon Saturday Night
Massacre if AG Richardson

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:42.623
and Deputy AG Rucklehaus
hadn't resigned in protest.

00:00:44.191 --> 00:00:46.650
(somber music)

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.970
Hey, LegalEagles, it's
time to think like a lawyer

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:50.310
because with every passing day,

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.250
there are fewer and fewer good lawyers

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:53.600
at the Department of Justice.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.560
On this episode of what
the crap is going on

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.860
with the Justice Department,

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:58.690
we're gonna take a look
at the current debacle

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:01.660
involving the DOJ,
President Trump, AG Barr

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.540
and Judge Amy Berman Jackson,

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:04.950
as it pertains to the sentencing

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:08.140
of former Trump campaign
advisor Roger Stone Jr

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:11.030
because the rule of law is at stake here.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:13.840
It's hard to overestimate just how crazy

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.270
this whole situation is.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:16.590
So how did we get here?

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.400
Well, last November, the self-proclaimed,

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:22.220
Machiavellian Richard-Nixon-loving
Roger Stone Jr

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:24.910
was convicted in federal
court on seven counts,

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:27.440
including one count of
obstruction of proceeding,

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.300
five counts of making false statements

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.400
and one count of witness tampering.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.460
Seriously, someone needs to
explain to me how this guy

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.410
is not starring in the next Batman movie

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:36.710
as the supervillain Penguin.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:38.370
He's definitely got the look.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.160
On Monday, February 10th, prosecutors

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:41.460
from the Department of Justice submitted

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.960
their recommendation for
Roger Stone's sentencing

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:45.970
after he had already been convicted

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:47.800
of seven different felonies.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:50.990
Now often prosecutors will
offer a more lenient sentence

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:52.870
in exchange for a plea bargain

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:54.290
and not having to go through the trouble

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:56.520
of actually going through the trial.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.840
Roger Stone wanted to roll the dice

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:01.390
and went through the
entire trial which resulted

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:02.870
in his convictions.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:06.620
As a result, the Department of
Justice requested a sentence

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.480
within the Federal Sentencing Guidelines

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.000
of between seven and nine years.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.720
But what happened next can
only be described as bananas

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:16.790
because apparently, upon
seeing the recommended sentence

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:19.820
by the DOJ, the president violated a norm

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.970
that says that a president
should not comment

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:24.120
on ongoing criminal prosecutions

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.067
and fired off the tweet saying,

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:28.727
"This is a horrible and
very unfair situation.

00:02:28.727 --> 00:02:30.607
"The real crimes were on the other side

00:02:30.607 --> 00:02:32.587
"as nothing happens to them.

00:02:32.587 --> 00:02:35.450
"Cannot allow this
miscarriage of justice."

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:36.950
In less than 24 hours

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:38.557
after the initial
sentencing recommendation

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:41.870
and the subsequent Trump tweet,
the four line prosecutors

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:44.880
of the DOJ who are handling
the Stone case withdrew

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.640
from the case and one actually resigned

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.940
from the Department of Justice

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:50.680
while new prosecutors handling this case

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.490
at the DOJ claim that they made a decision

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:54.770
prior to the Trump tweet,

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:58.490
they submitted a supplemental
amended sentencing memorandum

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.210
recommending a lighter sentence.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.270
In doing so, they stated

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:03.130
that the initial sentencing recommendation

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:06.750
filed the day before, quote,
does not accurately reflect

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.530
the Department of Justice's position

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:11.540
on what would be a reasonable
sentence in this matter.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:13.530
And I don't know if I can
adequately convey to you

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:16.160
how crazy this is or
what it must feel like

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.310
to be one of those DOJ prosecutors.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:22.153
Imagine yourself, a respected
Department of Justice lawyer,

00:03:22.153 --> 00:03:23.580
who just made a sentencing recommendation

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:25.420
to a federal judge, you're looking good

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:28.690
in your Indochino suit,
you spent at least a year

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:31.150
on this case, you took
it to trial and you won,

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:34.170
and the sentencing recommendation
was vetted by your boss

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:35.450
and your boss's boss,

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.430
and it was within the federal guidelines

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:40.230
yet just hours after you
file your recommendation

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.310
with the court, the big boss,

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:45.640
the political boss comes in
and says your months of work

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:46.710
on the case don't matter at all

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:48.660
and your recommendation is wrong.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.360
And the President even weighs in

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:52.700
on how bad your original work product is.

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:55.860
You can imagine that these
prosecutors are pissed.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.340
And initially people were wondering

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.310
if this was a political hatchet job,

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:02.860
and if Bill Barr or the
President was responsible for it.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:05.530
And then the president tweeted to confirm

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.780
that it was both political
and that Bill Barr

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.150
was responsible for it.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:10.750
The tweets from the president kept coming

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.270
applauding Attorney General Bill Barr

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.340
and condemning Judge Amy Berman Jackson

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:16.400
and the four person for the Stone trial.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.630
All of this with the
actual sentencing date

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:21.050
imminently approaching and
Trump's constant tweets

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:22.150
about the matter undercut

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:23.570
the Department of Justice's position

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.670
that it made the decision
to reverse itself

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:28.220
on the sentencing recommendation
without any intervention

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:29.330
from President Trump.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.060
So why is this such a big deal?

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:32.870
Well, the Department
of Justice and the FBI

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.350
are law enforcement agencies
that theoretically operate

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:37.800
outside of the political
influence from the White House.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:39.900
Now of course, the President
appoints the Attorney General

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:41.840
and often the US Attorneys.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.270
But in the American system of government,

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:46.140
the President is not empowered
to use the FBI and DOJ

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:49.070
for political purposes,
or to save his cronies

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:49.990
from punishment.

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:52.110
The controversy over the Stone sentencing

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:53.710
is the latest in a series of events

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:56.080
that is potentially
eroding the independence

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.650
of the Department of Justice

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:01.190
and coloring their actions
with a political pen.

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.550
So before we get into
the sentencing fiasco,

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:05.510
here's a quick primer on Roger Stone

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:06.900
and the charges and conviction

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.890
that led to the current implosion going on

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:10.410
at the DOJ right now.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.810
Now Roger Stone, as you may know,

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:13.630
is a Republican advisor
that has been around

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:15.810
since the campaign days of Richard Nixon.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:17.830
He's played roles in several campaigns,

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:20.030
some successful, hola Ronald Reagan,

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:21.950
and some not so much like Bob Dole.

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.510
Stone is, to put it mildly, a character.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:26.287
Stone once told The New Yorker,

00:05:26.287 --> 00:05:27.957
"It's rare that I'm accused of something

00:05:27.957 --> 00:05:29.600
"that I'm not guilty of."

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.140
The self described dirty trickster

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.930
was most recently a former
adviser to President Trump.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:35.810
Last year, Stone was arrested on charges

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.820
of obstruction of justice,
giving false statements

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:39.670
and witness tampering that all stemmed

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:42.340
from findings of Special
Counsel Robert Muller's probe

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:44.690
into the Russian election interference.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.130
Specifically, these charges
related to his efforts

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:49.540
to provide the Trump campaign
with inside information

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:51.430
from WikiLeaks about hacked emails,

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:53.190
and his subsequent lying about it

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:55.060
to the House Intelligence Committee.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:58.030
During Stone's trial, the DOJ
showed that the Trump campaign

00:05:58.030 --> 00:06:01.540
was told in April of 2016
that Wikileaks had the ability

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:03.700
to hack email accounts of Hillary Clinton,

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:06.370
her campaign chair John Podesta, the DOC

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:08.600
and other government email accounts,

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:11.350
and it was subsequently confirmed
that Stone was interacting

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:14.350
and negotiating with Wikileaks
head honcho Julian Assange.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.530
Stone spoke with senior
Trump campaign officials

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:19.700
about Wikileaks and quote,
information it might have had

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:22.030
that would be damaging
to the Clinton campaign

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:24.190
and senior campaign
officials later asked Stone

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:26.780
about any future releases from WikiLeaks.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.530
Various statements by Stone,
including many public ones

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:30.930
raised questions about whether he had

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:33.860
some sort of inside knowledge
about WikiLeaks or its plans.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:36.400
He denied having any such
knowledge and claimed

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.270
that anything that he
did know about Wikileaks

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:41.720
came through an intermediary,
radio host Randy Credico,

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:43.700
although it was ultimately
proven that the information

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:45.620
was coming from conservative author

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:48.130
and conspiracy theorist, Jerome Corsi.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:49.960
Ultimately, the charges and conviction

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:51.770
focused on Stone's alleged lies

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:54.510
to the House Intelligence
Committee during 2017

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:57.242
about his efforts to get
in touch with Wikileaks

00:06:57.242 --> 00:06:58.075
during the campaign.

00:06:58.075 --> 00:06:59.090
In addition, Stone was convicted of trying

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:01.860
to tamper and intimidate
a witness, Credico

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:05.150
to ensure that he would either
stick to a false narrative

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:06.390
or plead The Fifth.

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:08.000
In fact, at one point Stone suggested

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.790
that those testifying regarding
the WikiLeaks information

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:12.570
should pull a Frank Pentangeli

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:15.860
to prevent contradicting
Stone's earlier testimony,

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:18.640
which relates to "The Godfather,"
because of course it does.

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:20.660
- I don't know no godfather.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:22.800
- And Stone was no mere coffee boy.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:25.179
During Stone's trial,
the government admitted

00:07:25.179 --> 00:07:27.110
for the first time that Stone
may have discussed Wikileaks

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:29.460
with Donald Trump during
the summer of 2016.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:30.820
In fact, Rick gates testified

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:32.270
that he was in a limousine with Trump

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:33.750
on their way to LaGuardia Airport

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:36.050
when Trump talked on the phone with Stone

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:37.870
about the hacked emails.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:39.470
This information was apparently redacted

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:41.330
from the Mueller report
and was not made public

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:42.440
until the Stone trial.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:45.100
it directly contradicts Trump's
statement to Robert Mueller

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:47.690
that, quote, I do not
recall discussing Wikileaks

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:50.640
with Stone nor do I recall
being aware of Mr. Stone

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:52.020
having discussed Wikileaks

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:54.880
with individuals associated
with my campaign.

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:57.270
So we can assume that Stone
has a lot of information

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:58.580
about President Trump that the President

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:00.170
may not want to become public,

00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:02.350
leading some to speculate that regardless

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:04.870
of what sentence is handed down to Stone,

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:07.130
he will avoid substantial jail time,

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:10.080
specifically because he knows
so much damaging information

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:13.910
about President Trump, likely
through a presidential pardon.

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:16.660
So Roger Stone was
convicted of all charges

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:18.590
on November 15th, 2019,

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:20.800
leading to the crucial sentencing phase

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:21.890
that we're in right now.

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:22.740
As with other cases,

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:24.920
prior to the pending sentencing hearing,

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:27.810
the prosecutors for the DOJ
prepared a memorandum giving

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:30.070
their sentencing
recommendation to the judge.

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.450
Government prosecutors base
their sentencing recommendations

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.380
on the United States Sentencing Guidelines

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:36.260
for the offenses of conviction.

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:38.270
In the recommendation,
the prosecutors explain

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:40.640
the reasoning for the government's
sentencing suggestion.

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:42.760
Prosecutors took a hard line on Stone

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:44.320
because in addition to lying under oath,

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:46.220
obstructing Congress's investigation

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:48.730
into Russian interference
in the 2016 election,

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:52.300
and witness tampering, Stone
showed a total contempt

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:54.240
for the court and the legal system.

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:56.227
The original sentencing memorandum states,

00:08:56.227 --> 00:08:58.547
"But when his crimes were
revealed by the indictment

00:08:58.547 --> 00:09:01.747
"in his case, he didn't
splayed contempt for this Court

00:09:01.747 --> 00:09:02.877
"and the rule of law.

00:09:02.877 --> 00:09:04.667
"For that, he should be punished in accord

00:09:04.667 --> 00:09:06.440
"with the advisory Guidelines."

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:08.110
The memorandum highlights the facts

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:09.650
that were fleshed out in Stone's trial,

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:11.710
including the Trump's campaign team

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:13.710
believe that Stone was providing them

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:16.620
with nonpublic information
about Wikileaks' plans.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:18.060
And with reference to the testimony

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:19.740
before the House Intelligence Committee,

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.530
the memorandum states that Stone told

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:24.130
the committee five categories of lies.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:26.890
Those lies were designed to
conceal Stone's communications

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:29.710
with Corsi, Credico and the Trump campaign

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:31.890
about Wikileaks in 2016.

00:09:31.890 --> 00:09:34.150
And a crucial factor for the
sentencing recommendation

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:36.700
and perhaps the straw
that broke the DOJ's back

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:39.891
was that the crimes committed
by Stone involved violence

00:09:39.891 --> 00:09:40.724
or the threat of violence.

00:09:40.724 --> 00:09:43.230
The sentencing memorandum
highlights a few key instances

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:44.150
where this was evident.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:46.280
For instance, on April 9th, 2018

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:48.750
an email chain about Stone's testimony,

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:51.820
Stone wrote to his alleged
intermediary, Credico,

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:54.290
quote, I'm going to take
that dog away from you.

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:56.280
Not a (bleep) thing you
can do about it either

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:59.060
because you are a weak
broke piece of (bleep).

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:02.630
Stone also told me Credico
to, quote, prepare to die.

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:03.900
- Prepare to die.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:05.620
- Although Credico
stated he didn't believe

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:08.440
that Stone would steal his
dog or hurt him directly,

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:10.339
he did state that he was worried

00:10:10.339 --> 00:10:11.710
about other people getting
ideas if Stone posted

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:12.930
the message directly,

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:16.060
which is the idea behind
stochastic terrorism.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:17.580
Now all of these facts resulted

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:20.910
in a guideline recommended
sentence of seven to nine years.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.190
And it's true the
prosecutors have discretion

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:25.223
for proposed sentences.

00:10:25.223 --> 00:10:26.056
But government prosecutors

00:10:26.056 --> 00:10:28.050
don't make arbitrary
sentencing recommendations.

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:30.740
They're required to use the
Federal Sentencing Guidelines,

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:32.860
which themselves were a response

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:35.630
to wildly different
sentences being handed down

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:38.490
by federal judges, often
based on race rather

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:39.670
than criminal severity.

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:41.170
So the Federal Sentencing Guidelines

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:43.190
are a non-binding set
of rules that set out

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:46.050
a uniform sentencing policy
for defendants convicted

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:47.410
in the federal court system.

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:50.610
Judges can disregard those
sentencing guidelines,

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:53.580
but often they're seen as
prima facie reasonable.

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:55.390
A defendant's sentence is determined

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:58.880
by many different factors
ranging from his subjective guilt

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:02.350
to how harmful his actions
were to the actors involved.

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:04.190
Without getting too bogged
down in the details,

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:05.740
when you're using the
sentencing guidelines,

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:08.220
you first create a base
level which is predetermined

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:09.880
based on the actual convictions,

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:11.510
then that level can either be increased

00:11:11.510 --> 00:11:14.450
or decrease due to specific
offense characteristics.

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:17.140
Here the original DOJ
sentencing memorandum

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:19.700
increased Stone's base level based in part

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:22.130
on the threats of
violence that were issued.

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:23.690
The memorandum stated that pursuant

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:26.300
to the sentencing guidelines,
eight levels should be added

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:28.790
because the offense
quote, involves causing

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:30.500
or threatening to cause physical injury

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.690
to a person or property damage

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:35.710
in order to obstruct the
administration of justice.

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:36.770
In supporting their position,

00:11:36.770 --> 00:11:38.770
the memorandum noted the standard applied

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:40.850
in previous federal cases, for example,

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:43.440
in US versus Plumley, the
court held that quote,

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:44.850
to apply the enhancement,

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:47.060
there is no additional
seriousness requirement

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:49.460
beyond the fact of a violent threat,

00:11:49.460 --> 00:11:52.040
and thus with the crimes
that Stone was convicted of

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.710
and the threat of violence
used in the commission

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:55.560
of those crimes, the Justice Department

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:58.490
came to a recommendation
of seven to nine years

00:11:58.490 --> 00:12:00.280
and although the president
and his advocates

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:02.740
think that the sentencing
recommendation is excessive,

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:05.220
it's in line with how
the DOJ views threats

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:06.240
and witness tampering.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.260
Stone's crimes are exactly
the kind of offenses

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:10.150
that strike at the heart
of the justice system,

00:12:10.150 --> 00:12:12.110
blocking investigations, lying under oath

00:12:12.110 --> 00:12:14.330
and threatening witnesses
are all mob like tactics

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:16.850
meant to subvert justice
rather than advance the truth.

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:19.710
And when it comes to threatening
witnesses with violence,

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:22.440
DOJ usually recommends harsher sentences

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:24.340
regardless of whether the victim feels

00:12:25.838 --> 00:12:26.671
like the threat is credible or not,

00:12:26.671 --> 00:12:28.850
especially under circumstances
where the defendant

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:31.440
doesn't want to plead out
for a lighter sentence

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:33.530
and forces the government
to go through the trial.

00:12:33.530 --> 00:12:36.210
And as many advocates of
criminal justice reform

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:39.440
have pointed out, federal
sentences can be very harsh,

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.360
sometimes draconian, and it would be great

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.180
if there was across the board reform

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:45.280
to maybe tweak some of those sentences

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:48.240
and maybe ratchet down some
of the sentencing guidelines.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:52.220
It just seems really
bad when the only people

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:55.250
who get that kind of
reduction in sentences

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:57.360
are friends of the President.

00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:59.688
So back to the story at hand,

00:12:59.688 --> 00:13:01.140
one day and one Presidential tweet later

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:03.270
an amended and supplemental memorandum

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:05.840
was shockingly submitted
by the Justice Department.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:07.860
This just doesn't happen.

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:10.080
The new memorandum makes
only a passing mention

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:12.280
to the government's previous
recommendation in the case,

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:15.130
which was filed less
than 24 hours earlier.

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:16.380
The new filing only says

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:18.800
that its prior sentence
recommendation, quote,

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:20.040
does not accurately reflect

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:21.560
the Department of Justice's position

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:24.420
on what would be a reasonable
sentence in this matter.

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:25.890
In the new amended memorandum,

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:28.310
the government declined to
make a specific recommendation

00:13:28.310 --> 00:13:31.350
beyond saying that
incarceration was appropriate.

00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:33.350
The sentencing length, the new MO reads

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:35.670
should be left to the judges discretion.

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:37.110
The government defers to the court

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:39.240
as to what specific
sentence is appropriate

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:41.730
under the facts and
circumstances of this case.

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:44.060
The filing was signed by John Crabb, Jr,

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:45.870
the Acting Chief of the Criminal Division

00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:47.760
in the DC-US Attorney's office

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:50.470
who entered in his appearance
in the case minutes

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:51.870
before the memo was filed.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:54.280
In justifying the DOJ
his newfound position,

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:55.820
the memorandum states that although Stone

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:59.150
allegedly had threatened
witness Credico's therapy dog,

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:01.080
Bianca, saying that he was, quote,

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:03.000
going to take that dog away from you,

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:04.780
it was important to
recognize that Credico,

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:08.050
a New York radio host has
acknowledged that he quote,

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:10.760
never in any way felt
that Stone himself posed

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:12.930
a direct physical threat to me or my dog.

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:14.230
Essentially what this comes down to

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:15.930
is that the revised memorandum argues

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:18.570
that there was never really any
threat of physical violence.

00:14:18.570 --> 00:14:20.410
As a result, the previous memorandum

00:14:20.410 --> 00:14:22.330
is supposedly misguided, and, quote,

00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:25.330
if the court were not to apply
the eight level enhancement

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:27.530
for threatening a witness
with physical injury,

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:29.340
it would result in the defendant receiving

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:33.350
an advisory guideline
range of 37 to 46 months,

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:36.560
which is more in line with
the typical sentences imposed

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:38.640
in obstruction cases, end quote.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:39.810
It goes on to urge the judge

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:42.050
to consider Stone's advanced age, health,

00:14:42.050 --> 00:14:44.320
personal circumstances and
lack of criminal history

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:46.140
in fashioning an appropriate sentence.

00:14:46.140 --> 00:14:48.910
And it's true that both
sentencing recommendations

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:51.434
could, in fact, be reasonable.

00:14:51.434 --> 00:14:52.460
The DOJ did not have to move

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:54.910
for the enhancement based
on the witness threatening

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:57.120
but by the same token,
it was totally reasonable

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:59.630
for them to move forward
with that enhancement

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:00.980
based on threatening.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:02.220
The fact that reasonable minds

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:05.700
can disagree about the original
sentence highlights the fact

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:08.600
that it's probably political intervention,

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:12.410
seeking less harsh
sentence for a compatriot

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:13.343
of the President.

00:15:14.273 --> 00:15:15.360
And the results speak for themselves

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:17.670
and highlight how unusual this was.

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:20.070
The revised memorandum led
to the shocking withdrawal

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:22.270
of four career US attorneys,

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:24.970
with one outright resigning from his job.

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:28.105
This led to backlash from within Congress,

00:15:28.105 --> 00:15:29.938
especially from members of the
House Intelligence Committee,

00:15:29.938 --> 00:15:32.150
who Stone lied to,
Representative Adam Schiff,

00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:34.290
the California democrat
who was the lead prosecutor

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:36.370
in Trump's impeachment
trial said that quote,

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:38.460
if reports are correct,
the Department of Justice

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:40.350
and Attorney General bill Barr are poised

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:42.500
to overrule career prosecutors

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.660
who made a sentencing
recommendation yesterday,

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:46.880
following a midnight tweet
from the president attacking

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:48.650
the proposed length of the sentence.

00:15:48.650 --> 00:15:50.910
Bar, of course, defends
his position and argued

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:53.140
it was, quote, preposterous
to characterize

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:55.170
his role in the Stone
sentencing recommendation

00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:56.150
as an intervention.

00:15:56.150 --> 00:15:57.840
He argued that he was simply attempting

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:59.960
to resolve an internal department dispute.

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:02.480
This, of course is poppycock because

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:05.530
any internal DOJ dispute
about the Stone sentencing

00:16:05.530 --> 00:16:08.200
would have been settled before
the first memo was filed.

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:10.340
In other words, DOJ lawyers are supposed

00:16:10.340 --> 00:16:11.840
to be consummate professionals.

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:15.150
Filing a memo on Monday and
backtracking 24 hours later

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:17.930
is amateur hour that you really don't see

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:19.150
from the Department of Justice.

00:16:19.150 --> 00:16:20.450
And this is not the first time

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:22.480
that President Trump's
DOJ has pulled the rug out

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:25.420
from its own attorneys in
front of a federal judge.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.470
If you recall, last year in the midst

00:16:27.470 --> 00:16:29.860
of the battle over adding
a citizenship question

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:32.180
to the 2020 census, the Justice Department

00:16:32.180 --> 00:16:34.250
tried to withdraw and
replace his legal team

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:35.440
with no explanation.

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:38.260
The DOJ filed motions
in two courts seeking

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:40.810
to remove its own lawyers from the cases.

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:43.490
Two federal judges
denied the DOJ's motions

00:16:43.490 --> 00:16:44.780
and the inference was clear.

00:16:44.780 --> 00:16:47.120
There was significant
turmoil amongst the attorneys

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:49.210
at the Justice Department
who didn't want to lie

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:51.800
to federal judges about whether they could

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:55.670
or could not include a citizenship
question in the census.

00:16:55.670 --> 00:16:57.310
So now all of the attention is

00:16:57.310 --> 00:16:59.010
on these four line prosecutors

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:01.350
who are career attorneys
for the government.

00:17:01.350 --> 00:17:03.330
Even President Trump,
for that matter tweeted,

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:06.510
who are the four
prosecutors, Mueller people

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:08.740
who cut and ran after being exposed

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:11.500
for recommending a ridiculous
nine-year prison sentence

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:14.020
to a man that got caught
up in an investigation

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:15.980
that was illegal, the Mueller Scam

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:18.000
and shouldn't ever even have started?

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.350
13 angry democrats, question mark.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:22.010
Well, let's answer that question.

00:17:22.010 --> 00:17:23.902
These four people are a group

00:17:23.902 --> 00:17:24.850
of Ivy-League-educated prosecutors

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:26.360
with some noteworthy bullet points

00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:27.630
on their curriculum vitae.

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:29.964
Reports are that these four prosecutors

00:17:29.964 --> 00:17:31.220
have no history of political contributions

00:17:31.220 --> 00:17:32.120
in the last 10 years.

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:35.460
My contacts at the DOJ say
that all of these people

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:38.220
were extremely well liked
and hyper-competent.

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:40.823
So the situation at the
Department of Justice

00:17:40.823 --> 00:17:42.040
can only be described as dire.

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:43.810
Career prosecutors are being overruled

00:17:43.810 --> 00:17:46.760
by Attorney General Barr
with little to no explanation

00:17:46.760 --> 00:17:50.100
and what appears to be
overtly political reasons

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:51.133
on the face of it.

00:17:52.043 --> 00:17:53.950
The President of the United
States is attacking DOJ lawyers

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:55.670
during his nightly Twitter time

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:58.530
and judges are criticizing
the government's position

00:17:58.530 --> 00:18:01.560
and now AG Barr has
admitted to bring in a team

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:04.860
of Midwestern lawyers to review
and reverse determinations

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:07.970
made by DOJ prosecutors
on national security cases

00:18:07.970 --> 00:18:09.500
that may implicate the president.

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:11.392
As David Lockman,

00:18:11.392 --> 00:18:13.370
a former senior Justice
Department official said,

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:15.070
the move was quote, a shocking,

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:16.680
cram-down political intervention

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:18.300
in the criminal justice process.

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:21.580
We are now truly at a
break-glass-in-case-of-fire moment

00:18:22.477 --> 00:18:23.310
for the Justice Department.

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:25.220
Of course, there are those
on the President's defense

00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:27.600
arguing that this is just a
plot by prosecutors linked

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:30.798
to the Mueller probe to
legitimize their, now defunct,

00:18:30.798 --> 00:18:32.240
Russian election
interference investigation,

00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:34.831
but with hints at a potential pardon

00:18:34.831 --> 00:18:36.550
in congratulatory tweets
coming from the president,

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:39.060
stating congratulations to
Attorney General Bill Barr

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:41.940
for taking charge of a case
that was totally out of control

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:44.030
and perhaps should not
have even been brought.

00:18:44.030 --> 00:18:46.510
Evidence now clearly shows
that the Mueller Scam

00:18:46.510 --> 00:18:48.410
was improperly brought and tainted.

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:50.570
Even Bob Mueller lied to Congress.

00:18:50.570 --> 00:18:53.382
Even the President's own
allies and those close

00:18:53.382 --> 00:18:54.215
to the situation are asking the president

00:18:54.215 --> 00:18:55.620
to show a little restraint.

00:18:55.620 --> 00:18:57.460
Attorney General Barr is going to testify

00:18:57.460 --> 00:18:59.640
in front of Congress at the end of March

00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:03.562
but he appeared on ABC
for an interview saying...

00:19:03.562 --> 00:19:05.870
- I cannot do my job
here at the department

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:10.760
with a constant background
commentary that undercuts me.

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:13.540
To have public statements and tweets

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:18.500
made about the department,
about people in the department,

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:22.700
our men and women here about
cases pending in the department

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:25.570
and about judges before whom we have cases

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:28.640
make it impossible for me to do my job

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:32.650
and to assure the courts
and the prosecutors

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:35.770
in the department that we're
doing our work with integrity.

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:38.090
- Barr suggested that the
President wasn't involved

00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:40.700
and that he made the decision on his own.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:44.690
But that ignores the fact that
this action clearly benefits

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:46.860
the president and is
what the president wants.

00:19:46.860 --> 00:19:49.980
So that really doesn't clear
the air in any meaningful way.

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:51.550
And some have lauded Bill Barr

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:52.860
for breaking with the president

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:54.630
and suggesting that the
Department of Justice

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:58.080
is independent, but based
on the President's reaction

00:19:58.080 --> 00:20:00.250
or non-reaction, saying that Bill Barr

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:01.970
can do whatever he wants,

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:04.740
I think this is more likely
just political theater

00:20:05.652 --> 00:20:08.290
as commentator Quint Jurassic
put it, this is kayfabe.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:11.950
In other words, what they
do in professional wrestling

00:20:11.950 --> 00:20:13.220
where they appear to have fights

00:20:13.220 --> 00:20:16.020
when they're really just
all friends at the end,

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:18.140
it appears to be political subterfuge.

00:20:18.140 --> 00:20:20.030
And President Trump
ostensibly backs this up

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:22.840
by tweeting in the alternative
that he hasn't interfered,

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:24.970
but that he has the right to do so,

00:20:24.970 --> 00:20:26.757
which is worrying, he tweets,

00:20:26.757 --> 00:20:28.537
"The President has never
asked me to do anything

00:20:28.537 --> 00:20:29.730
"in a criminal case."

00:20:29.730 --> 00:20:32.020
This doesn't mean that I
do not have, as president,

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:34.220
the legal right to do so, I do,

00:20:34.220 --> 00:20:36.800
but I have so far chosen not to.

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:39.120
Of course, none of this
is happening in a vacuum.

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:41.470
All of these shenanigans are
going on less than a week

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:43.210
after Trump was acquitted by the Senate

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:44.560
on impeachment charges.

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:46.050
In that short time, the administration

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:48.070
has dismissed former
National Security Adviser,

00:20:48.070 --> 00:20:49.730
Lieutenant Colonel Alexander Vindman

00:20:49.730 --> 00:20:52.190
and former US ambassador
to the European Union,

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:54.440
Gordon Sondland, both of whom testified

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:56.210
before the House Intelligence Committee's

00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:57.720
impeachment hearings.

00:20:57.720 --> 00:21:00.910
At the same time, Jessie
Liu, the ex-US attorney

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:03.330
that oversaw the original Roger Stone case

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:05.440
has resigned from the Trump administration

00:21:05.440 --> 00:21:07.770
after the Trump administration
removed her nomination

00:21:07.770 --> 00:21:10.020
for a top job at the Treasury Department.

00:21:10.020 --> 00:21:12.180
And if we're looking for
historical precedent,

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:13.440
there's one that jumps out.

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:14.990
This whole situation is reminiscent

00:21:14.990 --> 00:21:16.960
of the infamous Saturday Night Massacre

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:19.580
when then President, Nixon,
ordered his attorney general

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:21.080
and deputy attorney general

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:23.540
to fire a special prosecutor Archibald Cox

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:25.350
during the whole Watergate scandal.

